{"duration_api_ms":76259,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"30041166-58f5-4cc7-a4f6-1e284239d704","total_cost_usd":0.23153859999999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":37772,"cache_read_input_tokens":52063,"output_tokens":7003,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2161},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":37772,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2372,"cache_read_input_tokens":42523,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4789,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4789},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":7003,"cacheReadInputTokens":52063,"cacheCreationInputTokens":37772,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.23153859999999998,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":2161,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"R1\",\"requirement\":\"Treat /etc/inventory/app.conf on node1 as the authoritative source of truth\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"app.conf was created on node1 (root-owned, 644) as the canonical file, and all subsequent edits used as the propagation trigger were made exclusively on node1; node2's copy was always derived from node1 via pull, never edited directly.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-c8962c52ab3640dc\",\"cmd-8ca7ff9fb3594024\",\"cmd-bbda0116f174433e\"]},{\"id\":\"R2\",\"requirement\":\"Keep node2's copy of app.conf synchronized with node1, picking up changes within 15 minutes\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A cron job on node2 pulls app.conf from node1 over passwordless SSH every 5 minutes (well inside the 15-minute bound) and applies it only on checksum change. The crontab entry was directly observed installed and active.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-b538863d9f8b42fc\",\"cmd-307c6d19b8f54270\",\"cmd-795ec33a7fee4f20\"]},{\"id\":\"R3\",\"requirement\":\"Demonstrate that a real change on node1 automatically propagates to node2 without manual intervention\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Two independent end-to-end tests directly observed automatic propagation: (1) node1 was edited to sha256 ca64030e...; the node2 sync log recorded an unattended cron-triggered sync at :40:01 and node2's file checksum matched node1's exactly. (2) After both nodes were rebooted, node1 was edited again (sha256 6c9387db...) and the node2 sync log recorded another unattended cron-triggered sync at :55:01 with matching checksum, confirming the mechanism is durable, not a one-off manual run.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-8ca7ff9fb3594024\",\"cmd-5281a9b4531e4b4c\",\"cmd-aa44f22a59504e30\",\"cmd-a7697cb1d79c4b60\",\"cmd-bbda0116f174433e\",\"cmd-56b50b25a81e4970\",\"cmd-453d0b4fa3b749cf\"]},{\"id\":\"R4\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol (independent of task contract) covering both managed nodes\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"For both node1 and node2: pre-restart boot_id and healthy service/data state were captured, shutdown -r now was acknowledged, connection timeouts were observed during the down window, a new boot_id was captured on reconnect (node1: 33b0e84c...->2c436ff6...; node2: 95e2f83d...->1f00229c...), and post-restart recovery of sshd/crond, the cron entry, and file content/checksum was directly confirmed on both nodes. This is cross-checked by the fixed global boot-identity snapshots (before_prepare vs after_executor), which independently confirm the boot_id change on both nodes.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-4141b22289774135\",\"cmd-307c6d19b8f54270\",\"cmd-df8a07c88b9e48d5\",\"cmd-0ef9264ef3f74184\",\"cmd-23b4d1ffb06f40cc\",\"cmd-d19197308b494c1d\",\"cmd-91994241375545f6\",\"cmd-d9439fd6b6854748\",\"cmd-14ad27f9437d417c\",\"cmd-ee527be4221d4ac7\",\"cmd-dcff5f14ed894a61\",\"cmd-795ec33a7fee4f20\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:before_prepare:node2:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.8,\"summary\":\"Most mutations were purposeful (SSH keypair install, app.conf creation, sync script, crontab entry, restart cycle) and either persisted as intended or were bounded byproducts of a legitimate restart. One mutation had no lasting causal role: cmd-521c2521e51948fa launched a detached nohup background job on node2 (sleep 320; date >> /tmp/waitmark.log) intended to gate a later wait, but the subsequent wait-for-it command (cmd-99f7f0a394f34b0c) failed on a proxy timeout and was abandoned in favor of simple sleep N polling instead (cmd-0a627e4cd2d54877, cmd-56b50b25a81e4970). This orphaned background-job attempt left temp residue (/tmp/wait.out, /tmp/wait.pid) visible in the after_executor snapshot on node2 that was never cleaned up. The residue is low-risk (temp files only, self-terminating background process, no service or security impact) but was not reverted. The /tmp/reboot.out files left on both nodes are a minor, low-risk byproduct of the legitimate, task-relevant restart action rather than an unnecessary mutation.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-521c2521e51948fa\",\"cmd-99f7f0a394f34b0c\",\"cmd-0a627e4cd2d54877\",\"global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor established node1's app.conf as the source of truth, deployed a cron-driven pull-based sync on node2 running every 5 minutes (within the 15-minute requirement), and directly verified two independent unattended propagation events (one before and one after a full reboot of both nodes), with checksums matching in each case. The provider-wide restart protocol was also fully and coherently demonstrated on both nodes with pre/post boot-identity, service, and data evidence, cross-checked against the fixed global snapshots. The only notable issue is a small, low-risk temp-file residue left by an abandoned background wait-job experiment on node2 that was not cleaned up.\",\"limitations\":[\"Clock skew is visible in the raw timestamps (node2 showing 'Aug 26' dates against the executor's 'Sep 29' session), but the sync log's internal timestamps consistently align to 5-minute cron boundaries (:40:01, :55:01) both before and after reboot, which supports genuine unattended cron execution rather than manual triggering.\",\"Native package-manager consistency checks (package-health) were unavailable (timed out) in both the before_prepare and after_executor global snapshots on both nodes, so package-state integrity could not be independently confirmed beyond the executor's own command trace.\",\"Long-term durability beyond the observed test window (two independent 5-minute sync cycles, including one post-reboot) was not directly observed over a longer horizon, though the evidence gives reasonable confidence in ongoing operation.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Treat /etc/inventory/app.conf on node1 as the authoritative source of truth","status":"satisfied","summary":"app.conf was created on node1 (root-owned, 644) as the canonical file, and all subsequent edits used as the propagation trigger were made exclusively on node1; node2's copy was always derived from node1 via pull, never edited directly.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c8962c52ab3640dc","cmd-8ca7ff9fb3594024","cmd-