ion events (one before and one after a full reboot of both nodes), with checksums matching in each case. The provider-wide restart protocol was also fully and coherently demonstrated on both nodes with pre/post boot-identity, service, and data evidence, cross-checked against the fixed global snapshots. The only notable issue is a small, low-risk temp-file residue left by an abandoned background wait-job experiment on node2 that was not cleaned up.","limitations":["Clock skew is visible in the raw timestamps (node2 showing 'Aug 26' dates against the executor's 'Sep 29' session), but the sync log's internal timestamps consistently align to 5-minute cron boundaries (:40:01, :55:01) both before and after reboot, which supports genuine unattended cron execution rather than manual triggering.","Native package-manager consistency checks (package-health) were unavailable (timed out) in both the before_prepare and after_executor global snapshots on both nodes, so package-state integrity could not be independently confirmed beyond the executor's own command trace.","Long-term durability beyond the observed test window (two independent 5-minute sync cycles, including one post-reboot) was not directly observed over a longer horizon, though the evidence gives reasonable confidence in ongoing operation."]},"ttft_ms":28068,"type":"result","duration_ms":76320,"uuid":"1007971f-8957-4629-a77c-d68e6c93161c","ttft_stream_ms":3445,"time_to_request_ms":50,"first_content_frame_ms":3445,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
